<mujoco model="xarm6_pusht_ycb_clutter">
  <!-- Push the T through household clutter -- single_obstacle's cube plus
       three YCB objects scattered around the workspace.

       IsaacGym conf/task/sim_task04.yaml, re-scaled onto the lab table and
       the measured T-block (see tee.xml's header).

       EVERY OBSTACLE KEEPS ITS SIZE. The YCB meshes are scans of real
       objects and the cube is a real 0.1 m cube; only the table and the T
       were oversized, so nothing here is rescaled. What moved is where
       they sit: the whole field is now confined to |y| <= 0.3, the middle
       third of the table, so the corridor's two ends (y = +/-0.4) are
       clear of clutter and the block only meets it once it is under way.

       Laid out so every lane is passable. Measured on the compiled scene,
       the free lanes across the table at each obstacle row are

           y = +0.20 (sugar)          0.183 / 0.442 m
           y =  0.00 (cube)           0.209 / 0.350 m
           y = -0.17 (mustard, spam)  0.152 / 0.351 / 0.099 m

       against an 0.089 m crossbar, so the block can get through on either
       side of every one of them. The cube must NOT move independently:
       `_TABLETOP_CUBE` is shared with single_obstacle.

       THE REAL YCB MESHES, WHERE THE SOURCE USES ONE. spamCan.urdf and
       mustardBottle.urdf both point at `nontextured.stl`, so those two are
       that mesh, vendored under assets/. dominoSugar.urdf does *not* --
       it declares `<box size="0.06 0.095 0.175"/>` -- so it stays a box
       here, which is the faithful reading, not a simplification.

       MJX collides a mesh as its convex hull, so `maxhullvert` caps that
       hull and `oim/utils/scenes.py` carries the matching 2D hull rather
       than a bounding box. That is a real gain for these two: the hull is
       0.82x the bounding box in plan for the can and 0.71x for the bottle,
       so the planner no longer refuses space the simulator allows.
       tests/test_scenes.py checks the two representations against each
       other, mesh hull included.

       Each mesh is pre-centred on its own bounding box when vendored, so
       `pos` below is that bbox's centre -- not the link origin, since the
       YCB meshes are not centred on it. -->
  <include file="common.xml"/>
  <include file="tee.xml"/>
  <include file="tee_start.xml"/>

  <asset>
    <!-- Paths are relative to *this* file, matching xarm6.xml's convention
         (a relative meshdir would resolve against the top-level file
         instead and break when this scene is included from elsewhere). -->
    <mesh name="spam_can" file="assets/spam_can.obj" maxhullvert="32"/>
    <mesh name="mustard_bottle" file="assets/mustard_bottle.obj"
      maxhullvert="32"/>
  </asset>

  <worldbody>
    <!-- Same camera as open_table (see its comment); shared verbatim by
         every tabletop scene except shelf_gap. -->
    <camera name="front" pos="1.5592 0.0000 0.6494"
      xyaxes="0.0000 1.0000 -0.0000 -0.4226 0.0000 0.9063"/>

    <!-- conf/actors/block.yaml, identical to single_obstacle's. -->
    <geom class="tabletop_obstacle" name="obs_box" type="box" size="0.05 0.05 0.05" pos="0.35 0.0 0.05"/>

    <!-- conf/actors/spamCan.yaml -> ycb/spamCan/nontextured.ply. Mesh bbox
         0.1021 x 0.0601 x 0.0835 m. Far side of the table, on the goal half
         of the clutter band. -->
    <geom class="tabletop_obstacle" name="spam_can" type="mesh"
      mesh="spam_can" pos="0.60 -0.16 0.0418"/>

    <!-- conf/actors/dominoSugar.yaml. This one is genuinely a box in the
         URDF (full size 0.06 x 0.095 x 0.175 m, centred on the link
         origin), with init_ori [0, -0.707, 0, 0.707] (xyzw) = -90 degrees
         about y, which lays it on its side: full extents become
         0.175 x 0.095 x 0.06. Written pre-rotated and axis-aligned here,
         which is the identical volume. Near side, on the start half of the
         clutter band: it is the first thing the block meets. -->
    <geom class="tabletop_obstacle" name="domino_sugar" type="box"
      size="0.0875 0.0475 0.0300" pos="0.22 0.20 0.0300"/>

    <!-- conf/actors/mustardBottle.yaml -> ycb/mustardBottle/nontextured.stl.
         Mesh bbox 0.0972 x 0.0666 x 0.1913 m. The tallest obstacle in any of
         these scenes, on the near side opposite the spam can so the two
         stagger rather than forming a second gate. -->
    <geom class="tabletop_obstacle" name="mustard_bottle" type="mesh"
      mesh="mustard_bottle" pos="0.15 -0.18 0.0957"/>
  </worldbody>
</mujoco>
